// Pipelining Hazards Reference

// Data Hazard: Read After Write (RAW)
I1: ADD R1, R2, R3    // WB stage writes R1
I2: SUB R4, R1, R5    // ID stage reads R1 (Stall/Forwarding needed)

// Control Hazard: Branch Delay
I3: BEQ R6, R7, Target // EX determines outcome
I4: Inst_A             // Speculative execution
I5: Inst_B

// Handling Techniques:
// Data: Forwarding/Bypassing (EX->ID path)
// Control: Branch Prediction (flush pipeline on mispredict)
// Control: Delayed Branch Slot (I4 is always executed)
